.TH USDLESS 1 "May 2026" "usdless 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usdless \- terminal USD (Universal Scene Description) viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usdless
.RI [ usdFile ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usdless
is a terminal-based viewer for USD (Universal Scene Description) files.
It renders 3D scenes using Unicode half-block characters or Braille dot patterns
with 24-bit ANSI colour directly in the terminal, powered by Hydra's rendering pipeline.
.PP
The default mode presents a split TUI with a scene-tree panel on the left and an
interactive 3D viewport on the right. A fullscreen simple mode is also available
for low-bandwidth connections or minimal terminals.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I usdFile
Path to the USD file to view. Accepted formats:
.BR .usd ", " .usda ", " .usdc ", " .usdz .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR \fI{halfblock,braille}\fR, \fB\-\-renderer\fR \fI{halfblock,braille}\fR
Set the render mode for the 3D viewport.
.RS
.TP
.B halfblock
(Default) Uses Unicode upper half-block characters (\fB\[u2580]\fR) with separate
foreground and background colours per cell. Fast, full 24-bit colour. Best for
general use.
.TP
.B braille
Uses Braille dot patterns for finer geometric detail at reduced colour depth.
Works best with small terminal fonts and a true-colour terminal.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-simple
Bypass the TUI and show a fullscreen 3D view only. Recommended for slow SSH
connections or weaker terminals.
.TP
.BI \-\-select " PRIMPATH"
Prim path to initially select in the scene tree (e.g.\&
.BR /World/Geom/Cube ).
.TP
.BI \-\-camera " CAMERA"
Camera to set the view to on open. May be given as a prim name or a full prim path.
Defaults to the first camera found in the scene.
.SS Legacy flags
The following short flags are kept for backward compatibility and map to their
.B \-\-renderer
equivalents:
.TP
.B \-hb
Equivalent to \fB\-\-renderer halfblock\fR.
.TP
.B \-b
Equivalent to \fB\-\-renderer braille\fR.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
The following bindings apply in TUI mode.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch focus between the scene-tree panel and the 3D viewport.
.TP
.B `
Toggle between fullscreen 3D view and the split TUI layout.
.TP
.B Arrow\ keys
Orbit the camera (when the 3D viewport is focused) or navigate the scene tree
(when the tree panel is focused).
.TP
.B Enter
Select the highlighted prim in the scene tree.
.TP
.BR Left " / " Right
Collapse or expand a node in the scene tree.
.TP
.BR w " / " s
Zoom the camera in or out.
.TP
.B f
Auto-frame all visible meshes.
.TP
.BR q " / " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open a USD archive in the default half-block mode:
.PP
.RS 4
.B usdless Hubble.usdz
.RE
.PP
Use Braille render mode:
.PP
.RS 4
.B usdless Hubble.usdz \-r braille
.RE
.PP
Open in simple (fullscreen) mode:
.PP
.RS 4
.B usdless scene.usda \-\-simple
.RE
.PP
Select a specific prim on startup:
.PP
.RS 4
.B usdless scene.usda \-\-select /World/Geom/Cube
.RE
.PP
Open with a named camera:
.PP
.RS 4
.B usdless scene.usda \-\-camera main_cam
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B usdless
does not read any environment variables directly.
A terminal with 24-bit true-colour support is strongly recommended (e.g.\&
.BR iTerm2 ", " kitty ", " Alacritty ", " WezTerm ).
Set
.B TERM
to
.B xterm-256color
or
.B xterm-direct
if your terminal profile does not advertise true-colour automatically.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, unrecognised flags, or failure to open the USD file.
